could be shipped): `. ./base.sh`, `hork__is_converged`, `. ./override.sh`,
`hork__is_converged`, `hork__is_converged 2>/dev/null`, `. ./base.sh`,
`hork__is_converged` -- run `dorc why` for the per-site detail (the apply runs
each anyway, to stay safe)
      [ book.sh:15:1
   15 | . ./base.sh
      | \_________/

   = help:  sm site runs `. ./base.sh`
hint: '.' (line 15) is unmodeled: it is the first wall -- an oracle vouching its convergence would elide it when converged; 6 more unmodeled walls -- dorc why
dorc: run `dorc why` for the per-site cause-chains, or `dorc why book.sh:N` to query a source line
#!/bin/sh
# dorc apply: the book, with already-converged/dead lines elided (value-preserving stand-in).

